  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Drawings Received 26/07/2010: 12055_02_02-P1, 12055_02_03/P1, 12055_02_04-P1, 12055_02_05-P1, 12055_02_07-P1, 12055_02_08-P1, 12055_02_09-P1, 12055_02_10-P1, 12055_02_11-P1, 12055_02_12-P1, 12055_02_13-P1 Statements: 26/07/2010 Design and Access Statement, Code for Sustainable Homes Description)   therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - The waste and recycled materials storage arrangements shown on the approved drawing shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 5 - No development shall take place until details shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority for a scheme of suitable ventilation and hermetically sealed glazing for windows and doors to  rooms of all dwellings.  The details shall be carried out as approved.",
    "Condition : 6 - No development shall take place until details have be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority for a scheme of acoustic insulation and any associated ventilation to ensure the maximum noise level to be permitted within dwellings with windows shut and any other necessary means of ventilation provided shall not exceed the \"good\" limits for bedrooms and \"reasonable\" for living rooms contained in BS8233:1999. These being LAeq,16hour = 40 dB in living rooms, and a night(07:00 - 23:00) LAeq,8hour = 30 dB and LAFmax = 45 dB in bedrooms, and a night LAeq,1hour = 45 dB in Kitchens, Bathrooms and Utility",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall take place until details have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority, for a scheme of reducing carbon emissions form the total energy needs (heat, cooling and power) of the development by 20% if technically possible, by the on-site generation of renewable energy.  The details shall be carried out as approved.",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place until details of a Sustainable Drainage Scheme, including measures for the harvesting of rainwater, the minimisation of water run-off from the building, by at least 50% of that of the undeveloped site, and the conservation and reuse as appropriate of other water supplies in the building have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  These details shall be carried out as approved.",
    "Condition : 9 - No dwelling shall be occupied until space has been laid out within the site in accordance with the approved plans.",
    "Condition : 10 - No dwelling shall be occupied until space has been laid out within the site in accordance with the approved plans.",
    "Condition : 11 - The parking, loading and turning spaces shown on the approved drawings shall be constructed and available for use before first occupation of any part of the development and such spaces shall not be used for any other purposes.",
    "Condition : 12 - The landscaping details shall be carried out as detailed on drawing 12055_02_13-P1",
    "Condition : 13 - The building shall not be occupied until a means of access for pedestrians has been constructed in accordance with the approved plans.",
    "Condition : 14 - All access doorway to the development shall have a minimum clear width of 900mm, a level surface or ramp between the pavement and the floor and a door handle of not more than 1m above ground level."
  ],
